; ==============================================================================
; 0xFCF000-0xFDE70E -- the 0xFCF000 module: a 17-entry dispatch table, 3,427
;                      bytes of tables including a 96-character SET, and 60 KB
;                      of code
; ==============================================================================
;
; ⚠ READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING A COVERAGE FIGURE.  Almost every label below is
; `sub_XXXXXX`, which is an ADDRESS and not a claim.  This span was converted
; because it is the largest contiguous run in prom_a that decodes cleanly, not
; because its meaning is known -- the same trade the 0xFE0000 block records.
;
; WHY THIS SPAN.  `python3 notes/prom_a_module_frontier.py` ranks the thunk run
; T_F41F54-T_F421A8 FIRST in prom_a: 150 slots, 145 of them unconverted, 59,752
; bytes of contiguous target range, and the second-ranked run T_F42320-T_F42380
; lands in the same `.incbin`.
;
; ★ WHAT THE LINEAR DECODE IS CERTIFIED BY, and it is a check that can fail:
; `python3 notes/prom_a_linear_decode_check.py 0xFCFDA7 0xFDE70F --offenders`
;   * the module's 179 prom_b directory slots name 178 DISTINCT targets (two
;     slots share 0xFDE1DD).  The check tests the 177 that lie inside
;     [0xFCFDA7, 0xFDE70F) and ALL 177 land exactly on an instruction boundary of
;     ONE decode that starts at 0xFCFDA7 -- 0 off-boundary; the 178th is
;     0xFDE70F itself, the span's end, checked separately as a boundary.
;     ★ The FIRST target, 0xFCFDA7, is what pins the start of the code: the byte
;     before it, 0xFCFDA6, is the top byte of the last pointer in the table
;     block, so the module's data and its code meet there;
;   * 0 call/calr from an instruction inside the span to an address that is not a
;     boundary;
;   * 0xFDE70F is an instruction boundary of a decode that runs PAST it;
;   * the only undecodable byte, 0xFD70E1, is inside JumpTable_FD70C5, declared
;     as data below.
;
; ★★ WHY THE SPAN STOPS AT 0xFDE70F AND NOT AT 0xFDFFFF.  0xFDE70F is the LAST
; directory target in the `.incbin`, and beyond it the decode cannot be trusted:
; * running the same check to 0xFE0000 FAILS -- 0xFE0000 is not a boundary of a
;   decode from 0xFCFDA7, and eight `call` sites in 0xFDFEE9-0xFDFF7A name
;   addresses (0xFD61E9, 0xFD6FEE, 0xFD763E) that are 1-2 bytes past one;
; * exhaustively: of the 128 possible decode starts in 0xFDFF80-0xFDFFFF, only
;   0xFDFFFD and 0xFDFFFF produce a decode in which 0xFE0000 is a boundary.  So
;   the last bytes of the `.incbin` carry something a linear decode cannot frame,
;   and 0xFDE70F-0xFDFFFF (6,385 bytes) is deliberately LEFT `.incbin`.
;   Converting it would have put invented instructions in this file, which the
;   byte gate cannot see.
;
; THE MODULE'S SHAPE
;   0xFCF000  17 LE32 dispatch entries (this table)
;   0xFCF044  3,427 bytes of tables -- framed by their readers below
;             (this span was `ModuleTables_FCF044` until 2026-09-25)
;   0xFCFDA7  code, to 0xFDE70E
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; DispatchTable_FCF000 -- 17 LE32 code addresses
;
; Read by: ONE site, `add XBC,0x00FCF000 / ld XBC,(XBC)` at 0xFCFE1D-0xFCFE23,
;          followed by `lda XIY,(0xFCFE2D) / push XIY / jp (XBC)` -- a computed
;          CALL: the return address is pushed by hand before the jump.
; ENTRY COUNT 17, and ⚠ IT IS NOT BOUND-DERIVED.  The reader computes its index
;          with a multiply and NO compare, so unlike every other table in this
;          image the ROM does not state the count.  17 is taken from the DATA:
;          word 17, at 0xFCF044, is 0x00000000 -- not an address -- and the bytes
;          after it are a monotone ramp, i.e. a different table.  ★ LAST-ENTRY
;          TEST: entry 16 is 0x00FD6C93 and entry 0 is 0x00FCFE42, the first
;          instruction after the dispatcher's own block.  Recorded as WEAKER
;          evidence than a bound; do not quote it as if the ROM checked it.
; Evidence: three of the seventeen entries hold the same address, 0x00FD6C93 --
;          the shape of a default arm -- and the other fourteen are distinct and
;          ascending.
; Unknown:  what the seventeen operations are.
; ⚠ CORRECTION 2026-09-25 (lane proma): the count IS bound, one step
;          removed.  The reader, ScreenButton_SoundEditMenu, first calls
;          PanelEvent_ToFieldIndex (0xFD7905), which returns WA=0 only after
;          storing an operation in 0..16 at (XIZ-4) -- the byte this reader
;          multiplies -- and the reader skips the dispatch on 0xFFFF.  And
;          word 17 (0xFCF044), 0x00000000, is not the start of another table:
;          it is the zero word that ends all 38 tables of this shape framed below.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
DispatchTable_FCF000:
