;          reach it as `push <return>` + `jp (XIX)`.
; Inputs:  none -- 0x96 = 150 is the literal it pushes.
; Outputs: returns after the tick counter has advanced 150; BC clobbered by the
;          `popw bc` that pops the argument.
; Evidence: the whole body is `pushw 0x96 / calr Delay_Ticks / popw bc / ret`,
;          and `calr 0x000a` at 0xFE1414 lands on 0xFE1421 = Delay_Ticks.
; Unknown:  nothing here.  For what 307 ms is FOR see
;          notes/FINDINGS-prom_a-gap-T-pa3.md.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Delay_150Ticks:
	pushw 0x96                                           ; FE1411  0b 96 00
	calr Delay_Ticks                                            ; FE1414  1e 0a 00
	popw bc                                              ; FE1417  49
	ret                                                  ; FE1418  0e
