; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Fdc_ClassifyCommandOpcode -- is (0x605A18) a command this controller has?
;
; Called from: 1 site(s) in the module: Fdc_IssueCommand
; Inputs:  (0x605A18), the opcode byte.
; Outputs: L = 0 accepted, 1 rejected.
; Evidence: ★ THIS IS THE ROUTINE THAT NAMES THE DEVICE.  It masks the opcode
;          with 0x1F -- so MT, MFM and SK are ignored -- and accepts 0x1D,
;          0x19, 0x02..0x0A, plus whichever of
;          0x0B..0x11 the seven-entry Fdc_OpcodeValidityJumpTable admits, which
;          is 0x0C, 0x0D, 0x0F and 0x11.  The accepted set is therefore
;
;            {02 03 04 05 06 07 08 09 0A 0C 0D 0F 11 19 1D}   -- 15 opcodes
;
;          and the rejected set is the other 17 values of the 5-bit field.
;          That is EXACTLY the truth table of
;          `upd765_family_device::check_command()`
;          (../mame/src/devices/machine/upd765.cpp:1433-1478): every accepted
;          value is a uPD765 command and every rejected value is not.
;          notes/prom_a_fdc_checks.py builds both sets -- ours by simulating
;          this routine's constants as read back from the ROM, MAME's from the
;          case labels in upd765.cpp -- and fails unless all 32 values agree.
;          ⚠ CORRECTED 2026-08-25 (audit F14): the first sentence used to add
;          that masking with 0x1F "is how a uPD765 decodes".  The cited file says
;          the OPPOSITE four lines above the function it cites -- "The real 765
;          completely decodes the commands that don't have variable upper bits"
;          (upd765.cpp:1427-1429) -- and MAME's own switch matches 0x03, 0x04,
;          0x07, 0x08 and 0x0F whole, masking with 0x1F only for the ten commands
;          that carry MT/MFM/SK.  The mask is THIS DRIVER's shortcut, not the
;          chip's decode, and it is not what names the part.  What names the part
;          is the truth table above, which is unaffected: the firmware never
;          sends a fixed-opcode command with a top bit set, so the shortcut and
;          the real decode agree on every byte this driver actually issues.
; Unknown:  nothing here.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Fdc_ClassifyCommandOpcode:
.LFE5CE8:
