; 0xFE69BF-0xFE7732 -- THE DISK FORMAT MODULE, and four filesystem templates
; ==============================================================================
;
; Converted 2026-08-25.  Chosen because `notes/prom_a_xref.py 0xF42D38` puts
; SIXTEEN of the seventeen call sites of the FDC request veneer inside
; 0xFE6E84-0xFE7732 -- the largest concentration of disk traffic anywhere in
; either image -- and because two emulation gaps (T, the drive-motor line, and
; V, "how does a user reach Fdc_Request at all") name this module as the place
; to look.  See notes/FINDINGS-prom_a-disk-format.md.
;
; The module is in two halves.  0xFE69BF-0xFE6E3A is DATA: a complete x86 FAT16
; boot sector and a complete x86 master boot record, for a FIXED DISK, followed
; by 123 bytes whose framing is not established.  0xFE6E84-0xFE7732 is CODE:
; the routine that builds a floppy filesystem image in RAM and the routine that
; writes it to a freshly formatted disk, in a 720 KB and a 1.44 MB variant.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; DiskImage_HardDisk_BootSector -- 512 bytes, a DOS FAT16 boot sector
;
; Evidence, and it is arithmetic rather than resemblance.  Every field of the
; standard BIOS Parameter Block is present, in its standard place, and the
; four independent size statements AGREE:
;
;   +0x00  EB 3C 90              x86 JMP SHORT +0x3C / NOP -- the FAT entry
;   +0x03  " EMID2.0"            OEM name, 8 bytes
;   +0x0B  512                   bytes per sector
;   +0x0D  8                     sectors per cluster
;   +0x0E  1                     reserved sectors
;   +0x10  2                     number of FATs
;   +0x11  512                   root directory entries
;   +0x13  0                     total sectors, 16-bit field (0 => use +0x20)
;   +0x15  0xF8                  media descriptor -- 0xF8 is FIXED DISK
;   +0x16  250                   sectors per FAT
;   +0x18  60                    sectors per track
;   +0x1A  15                    heads
;   +0x1C  60                    hidden sectors
;   +0x20  511140                total sectors, 32-bit field
;   +0x24  0x80                  BIOS drive number -- 0x80 is the FIRST HARD DISK
;   +0x26  0x29                  extended boot signature
;   +0x27  EF 0F 20 1B           volume serial number
;   +0x2B  11 spaces             volume label
;   +0x36  "FAT16   "            filesystem type
;   +0x3E  x86 boot code, with the strings "Non-System disk or disk error",
;          "This is Technics HDD." and the CR/LF pairs around them
;   +0x1FE 55 AA                 boot signature
;
; ★ THE ARITHMETIC CHECK, which is what makes this a decode and not a guess:
;   511140 + 60 hidden = 511200 = 568 x 15 x 60 EXACTLY -- a whole number of
;   cylinders on the geometry the same sector states.  Capacity 511200 x 512 =
;   261,734,400 bytes, i.e. a ~250 MiB hard disk.  And the partition entry in
;   the master boot record below repeats BOTH numbers independently.
;
; ★ SO THIS NAMES UNIT 1.  `Fdc_Request`'s unit field selects a second storage
;   back end at 0x7E0008 whose PART is unknown (emulation gap J).  A FAT16 boot
;   sector for a fixed disk, a matching MBR, and the string "This is Technics
;   HDD." are the first thing in either image to say what the second unit IS.
;   Stated as strong evidence, NOT as proof: see Unknown below.
;
; Unknown:  ⚠ NO CONSUMER IS LOCATED.  Two searches were run and both are
;          empty -- `notes/prom_a_xref.py 0xFE69BF` (and 0xFE6BBF, 0xFE6DBF),
;          and a raw scan of prom_a AND prom_b for the three little-endian
;          address bytes.  So nothing in this tree copies these 1024 bytes
;          anywhere, and whether the firmware can format a hard disk at all is
;          NOT established by this data.  What IS established is that the ROM
;          carries the images.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
