; Disk_Format720K -- FORMAT a 720 KB floppy and write the filesystem onto it
;
; Called from: `calr` at 0xFE7217, inside Disk_FormatSelectedMedia, and nowhere
;          else that `notes/prom_a_ringbuf_map.all_refs()` finds.
; Inputs:  the RAM buffer at 0x60A080, already filled by DiskImage_Build720K.
; Outputs: A = 0 on success, else the FDC layer's error code; the request block
;          at RAM 0x17C0 is left holding the last request.
; Evidence: SEVEN requests, each built as a 16-byte block at 0x17C0 in the
;          field order Fdc_Request's own header gives (+0 op, +2 unit, +4 head,
;          +6 track or media, +8 first sector, +0x0A count, +0x0C buffer) and
;          each passed to the veneer 0xF42D38 -> 0xFE3018 -> Fdc_Request, with
;          `cp A,0 / jr NZ` abandoning the sequence on the first error:
;
;    #  op  unit head trk/media sec cnt buffer      what
;    1   0    0    0    0xE0     1   1  0           reset + identify media
;    2   5    0    0    0        1   1  0           FORMAT DISK
;    3   4    0    0    0        1   1  0x60A080    write boot sector
;    4   4    0    0    0        2   3  0x60A280    write FAT 1
;    5   4    0    0    0        5   3  0x60A280    write FAT 2, same source
;    6   3    0    0    0x4F     9   1  0x60A080    verify read, last track
;    7   3    0    0    0        9   1  0x60A080    verify read, track 0
;
