;   agree:
;   1. media descriptor 0xE0; `Fdc_MediaTypeJumpTable` (0xFE6E3A) indexes on
;      `& 0x0F`, so 0xE0 selects geometry 0, which
;      notes/FINDINGS-prom_a-fdc.md sec.4 reads off the ROM's own immediates as
;      512 bytes x 9 sectors;
;   2. the verify reads ask for SECTOR 9 on tracks 0x4F (79) and 0 -- the last
;      sector of a 9-sector track, and track 79 is the last of 80;
;   3. the boot sector this writes (BootSector_Floppy720K, 0xFE76B2) states
;      1440 total sectors, 9 per track, 2 heads, media 0xF9, 3 sectors per FAT
;      -- and requests 4 and 5 write exactly 3 sectors each, at 2 and at 5,
;      which is where two 3-sector FATs land after a 1-sector boot record.
;   Nothing here is inferred from the routine's position or from resemblance.
; Unknown:  why the head field is 0 for every request when the geometry has two
;          heads -- the FDC layer's own operation 5 arm may walk heads itself;
;          that is not checked here.
