; Disk_Format1440K -- FORMAT a 1.44 MB floppy and write the filesystem onto it
;
; Called from: `calr` at 0xFE720D, inside Disk_FormatSelectedMedia, and nowhere
;          else that `notes/prom_a_ringbuf_map.all_refs()` finds.
; Inputs:  the RAM buffer at 0x60A080, already filled by DiskImage_Build1440K.
; Outputs: A = 0 on success, else the FDC layer's error code.
; Evidence: NINE requests, same shape as Disk_Format720K, same abandon-on-error:
;
;    #  op  unit head trk/media sec cnt buffer      what
;    1   0    0    0    0xC3     1   1  0           reset + identify media
;    2   5    0    0    0        1   1  0           FORMAT DISK
;    3   4    0    0    0        1   1  0x60A080    write boot sector
;    4   4    0    0    0        2   5  0x60A280    write FAT 1, first 5
;    5   4    0    0    0        7   4  0x60A480    write FAT 1, last 4
;    6   4    0    0    0       11   5  0x60A280    write FAT 2, first 5
;    7   4    0    0    0       16   4  0x60A480    write FAT 2, last 4
;    8   3    0    0    0x4F    18   1  0x60A080    verify read, last track
;    9   3    0    0    0        9   1  0x60A080    verify read, track 0
;
; ★ WHY "1.44 MB", by the same three-way agreement:
;   1. media descriptor 0xC3, and 0xC3 & 0x0F = 3 selects geometry 3, which
;      FINDINGS-prom_a-fdc.md sec.4 reads as 512 bytes x 18 sectors;
;   2. the first verify read asks for SECTOR 18 of track 79;
;   3. BootSector_Floppy1440K (0xFE76F2) states 2880 total sectors, 18 per
;      track, 2 heads, media 0xF0, 9 sectors per FAT -- and requests 4+5 write
;      5+4 = 9 sectors starting at 2, requests 6+7 another 9 starting at 11,
;      which is exactly two 9-sector FATs after a 1-sector boot record.
; Unknown:  requests 5 and 7 take their source 512 bytes further into the image
;          than requests 4 and 6 end, so the second half of each FAT is written
;          from an overlapping slice.  Harmless -- the whole area past the
;          3-byte FAT ID is zero -- but it is not obviously intentional and is
;          recorded rather than explained.
